  "attack_chain": [],
  "evidences": [
    {
      "id": "ev_2",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s1"
      },
      "text": "Insikt Group analyzed the HermeticWiper malware and the associated ransomware component named PartyTicket that were first publicly reported targeting Ukrainian organizations on February 23, 2022.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_4",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s3"
      },
      "text": "Key Judgments • The use of a wiper malware with an associated destructive ransomware component is similar in method to WhisperGate, NotPetya, and other operations credited to Sandworm.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_5",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s4"
      },
      "text": "• There is insufficient evidence at this time to attribute HermeticWiper to the Russian state, but the timing of the mass deployment of HermeticWiper with kinetic attacks and other cyberattacks on Ukraine, and a methodology similar to past attacks by Russian government- associated actors, lends credence to such an attribution.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_6",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s5"
      },
      "text": "• The PartyTicket ransomware attacks are unlikely to be a true ransomware campaign conducted for financial gain.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_7",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "executive_summary",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s6"
      },
      "text": "It is more likely that the ransomware component is a ruse and the real purpose of the attacks are disruption and data destruction.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_8",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s7"
      },
      "text": "This report is a technical overview of the HermeticWiper and PartyTicket malware reported by ESET and Symantec on February 23, 2022.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_11",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 2,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p2_s10"
      },
      "text": "HermeticWiper, also known as FoxBlade, is a data wiper found targeting finance and government contractor organizations in Ukraine, Latvia, and Lithuania, according to Symantec .",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_17",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s2"
      },
      "text": "Although no direct attribution of HermeticWiper has been made by security researchers at this time, the timing being coincident with other cyberattacks and physical attacks on Ukraine and a history of similar tactics by Russian state- associated actors in their use of data wipers in the past, including WhisperGate in January 2022 and NotPetya in 2017 , suggest the involvement of a Russian state operation.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_22",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s7"
      },
      "text": "A Lithuanian organization that received HermeticWiper was initially compromised in November 2021.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_26",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s11"
      },
      "text": "The victims received a ransomware notification providing 2 email addresses: vote2024forjb@protonmail[.]com and stephanie.jones2024@ protonmail[.]com.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_28",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s13"
      },
      "text": "WhisperGate attacks used a similar methodology, wherein the attack was disguised as ransomware.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_29",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 3,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p3_s14"
      },
      "text": "Both WhisperGate and HermeticWiper used separate components to prevent a victim’s system from booting and file corruption; however, the component that played the role of ransomware changed between the 2 attacks.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_48",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s1"
      },
      "text": "PartyTicket Insikt Group analyzed the ransomware associated with the HermeticWiper malware, dubbed PartyTicket.",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
    {
      "id": "ev_50",
      "evidence_type": "report_text",
      "report_id": "RecordedFuture_mtp-2022-0302(03-02-2022)",
      "locator": {
        "page": 6,
        "section": "body",
        "sentence_id": "p6_s3"
      },
      "text": "Similarly, the ransom note dropped by the malware contained email addresses on similar topics, and the encrypted files were renamed with the suffix “[vote2024forjb@protonmail[.]com].",
      "language": "en",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "note": "narrative sentence evidence",
      "source": "document"
    },
